{"5028910":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"PlayCard Football","steam_appid":5028910,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"detailed_description":"<h1>News and Updates<\/h1><p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Demo out there for demonstration of the unique game design of PlayCard football.  Play at the high school level for 4 games!  Can level up and add cards to your playdeck!<\/p><\/p><br><h1>About the Game<\/h1><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You are the head coach.<\/strong> Not a player, not just a GM.  The coach on the sideline calling the shots. Every snap, you read the defense, pick your play from your hand, and watch your units implement it. <\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Every play is a decision.<\/strong> Your deck is your playbook. Spend tokens on the big-swing calls or save them for the grind. But lean on the same play too often and the defense catches on, the game punishes predictability.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Build a program, not just a run.<\/strong> Start on Friday nights in high school. Recruit, develop your units, and level your coach up.  If you're up to the challenge, take the promotion to college ball, then the pros. Move up and take your new team to success, your coach profile carries everything: levels, your coaching XP, the plays you've mastered. Your knowledge compounds while your roster and opponents change. Manage yourself, your team and your plays, and then you can experience the victory.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>COMPLETELY NEW WAY TO PLAY FOOTBALL<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/extras\/a47cc49d3f805fb1d513d14fbbbd970d.avif?t=1793637442\" width=1000 height=400 \/><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>EVERY SNAP IS A READ<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pre-snap, the defense shows you a picture  the shell, the box, the front, the pressure. Some of it is true. Some of it is bait. The smarter your quarterback, the deeper you see: rookie QBs get the shell; veterans sniff out man-or-zone before the ball is up. Trust the read and check into the right call, or get caught holding a screen pass against a coverage that eats it alive.<\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Disguised coverages that lie to bad quarterbacks and confess to great ones<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A limited audible budget — burn your checks early or save them for the two-minute drill<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Token-limited play calling: your best calls cost resources, so every series is a budget decision<\/p><\/li><\/ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Plays that beat man, plays that beat zone, and defenses that know which is which<\/p><\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>COACH A WHOLE CAREER<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Start on a Friday-night sideline. End — maybe — holding a pro trophy. This is not a run you restart; it's a career you live with.<\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Three leagues, one career:<\/strong> high school, college conferences, and a pro league with divisions, full schedules, and playoffs<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Promotion is your choice:<\/strong> dominate and move up, or stay and build a dynasty where you are<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Every game in the league is really played<\/strong> — rivals win, lose, rebuild, and peak on their own cycles; check the standings, the schedule, and your coaching record<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Build your program:<\/strong> a five-branch Coaching Tree, training and medical staff that keep your roster on the field, injuries that test your depth chart, and development calls that turn three-stars into cornerstones<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Your history follows you:<\/strong> season records, program milestones, and the players who came through your building<\/p><\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>HOW A SNAP WORKS<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Both hands are dealt face up. You can see cards the defense is holding, and they can see yours, but knowing what they <i>can<\/i> call still leaves you guessing what they <i>will<\/i>.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A card is one play, and everything you need is on the face: <strong>run or pass<\/strong>, the thing the defense is trying to guess; <strong>a rating out of 100<\/strong>, on the same scale as your players; <strong>a token cost<\/strong>, three a drive, so your best calls can't be your every-down calls; and <strong>the matchup it's built for<\/strong> — screens eat blitzes, deep shots punish an empty middle.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Then your roster runs it. The card says what to call; your players decide how well it goes. The same inside zone is a survival play behind a rebuilt line and a weapon behind a veteran one.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/extras\/579a8c40b0f48fa278c59c09ef1a6bf6.avif?t=1793637442\" width=1000 height=390 \/><\/span><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Both cards flip and the snap lands somewhere: <strong>stuffed<\/strong> and you're back a zone, <strong>short<\/strong> and you got nothing, <strong>gain<\/strong> and you're a zone closer, <strong>big play<\/strong> for two, <strong>explosive<\/strong> for three — the most any single snap can move the ball.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>TWO SNAPS<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Same defensive call both times — a <strong>Run Blitz<\/strong>, eight in the box, coming downhill. The only thing that changes is what the offense does about it.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Inside Zone into the Run Blitz — the defense wins.<\/strong> You ran at the one front built to stop it. No crease, the back is met at the line, and you're backed up with a down gone. <i>Stuffed. Zone 2 to Zone 1.<\/i><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/extras\/0328c87c3566944712391077987846a0.avif?t=1793637442\" width=1000 height=470 \/><\/span><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  <\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Play Action into the same Run Blitz — the offense wins.<\/strong> You showed run, they bit, and everyone they'd need in coverage is coming downhill instead. <i>Big play. Zone 2 to Zone 4.<\/i><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/extras\/a6d362c119634f44153a3da9cff88e7e.avif?t=1793637442\" width=1000 height=470 \/><\/span><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One card beat that blitz and one card fed it. The ratings barely moved — the difference was the read.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The field is five zones and an end zone, and a series is four plays. Scoring is something you assemble: a touchdown is a run of good calls, and the drive you remember is the one where you won three reads in a row.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/extras\/be5f0d82ab5751999fc76846fecdf7f2.avif?t=1793637442\" width=1000 height=180 \/><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>YOUR PLAYBOOK IS YOUR DECK<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Build your playbook like a coach installs an offense. Earn new plays as your career grows, and rep the ones you trust, plays gain mastery the more you call them, and a play your team has mastered hits harder than one you installed on Tuesday. Scout the opponent's tendencies, check the matchup screen, and bring the right game plan to the right opponent.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every call costs. A per-series token budget means your best looks can't be your every-down looks, the personnel you declare changes what you can afford, and your audibles are a finite resource you can burn early or save for the two-minute drill.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>FOOTBALL, ALL THE WAY DOWN<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Two-point decisions after a late touchdown. Safeties when a stuff goes wrong deep in your own end. Victory formation when you've iced it — or a handshake from a coach who knows you have. If it matters on a real sideline, it matters here.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>If you know football, this game was built for you. <\/strong><\/p>","about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You are the head coach.<\/strong> Not a player, not just a GM.  The coach on the sideline calling the shots. Every snap, you read the defense, pick your play from your hand, and watch your units implement it. <\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Every play is a decision.<\/strong> Your deck is your playbook. Spend tokens on the big-swing calls or save them for the grind. But lean on the same play too often and the defense catches on, the game punishes predictability.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Build a program, not just a run.<\/strong> Start on Friday nights in high school. Recruit, develop your units, and level your coach up.  If you're up to the challenge, take the promotion to college ball, then the pros. Move up and take your new team to success, your coach profile carries everything: levels, your coaching XP, the plays you've mastered. Your knowledge compounds while your roster and opponents change. Manage yourself, your team and your plays, and then you can experience the victory.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>COMPLETELY NEW WAY TO PLAY FOOTBALL<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/extras\/a47cc49d3f805fb1d513d14fbbbd970d.avif?t=1793637442\" width=1000 height=400 \/><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>EVERY SNAP IS A READ<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pre-snap, the defense shows you a picture  the shell, the box, the front, the pressure. Some of it is true. Some of it is bait. The smarter your quarterback, the deeper you see: rookie QBs get the shell; veterans sniff out man-or-zone before the ball is up. Trust the read and check into the right call, or get caught holding a screen pass against a coverage that eats it alive.<\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Disguised coverages that lie to bad quarterbacks and confess to great ones<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A limited audible budget — burn your checks early or save them for the two-minute drill<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Token-limited play calling: your best calls cost resources, so every series is a budget decision<\/p><\/li><\/ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Plays that beat man, plays that beat zone, and defenses that know which is which<\/p><\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>COACH A WHOLE CAREER<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Start on a Friday-night sideline. End — maybe — holding a pro trophy. This is not a run you restart; it's a career you live with.<\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Three leagues, one career:<\/strong> high school, college conferences, and a pro league with divisions, full schedules, and playoffs<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Promotion is your choice:<\/strong> dominate and move up, or stay and build a dynasty where you are<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Every game in the league is really played<\/strong> — rivals win, lose, rebuild, and peak on their own cycles; check the standings, the schedule, and your coaching record<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Build your program:<\/strong> a five-branch Coaching Tree, training and medical staff that keep your roster on the field, injuries that test your depth chart, and development calls that turn three-stars into cornerstones<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Your history follows you:<\/strong> season records, program milestones, and the players who came through your building<\/p><\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>HOW A SNAP WORKS<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Both hands are dealt face up. You can see cards the defense is holding, and they can see yours, but knowing what they <i>can<\/i> call still leaves you guessing what they <i>will<\/i>.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A card is one play, and everything you need is on the face: <strong>run or pass<\/strong>, the thing the defense is trying to guess; <strong>a rating out of 100<\/strong>, on the same scale as your players; <strong>a token cost<\/strong>, three a drive, so your best calls can't be your every-down calls; and <strong>the matchup it's built for<\/strong> — screens eat blitzes, deep shots punish an empty middle.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Then your roster runs it. The card says what to call; your players decide how well it goes. The same inside zone is a survival play behind a rebuilt line and a weapon behind a veteran one.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/extras\/579a8c40b0f48fa278c59c09ef1a6bf6.avif?t=1793637442\" width=1000 height=390 \/><\/span><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Both cards flip and the snap lands somewhere: <strong>stuffed<\/strong> and you're back a zone, <strong>short<\/strong> and you got nothing, <strong>gain<\/strong> and you're a zone closer, <strong>big play<\/strong> for two, <strong>explosive<\/strong> for three — the most any single snap can move the ball.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>TWO SNAPS<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Same defensive call both times — a <strong>Run Blitz<\/strong>, eight in the box, coming downhill. The only thing that changes is what the offense does about it.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Inside Zone into the Run Blitz — the defense wins.<\/strong> You ran at the one front built to stop it. No crease, the back is met at the line, and you're backed up with a down gone. <i>Stuffed. Zone 2 to Zone 1.<\/i><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/extras\/0328c87c3566944712391077987846a0.avif?t=1793637442\" width=1000 height=470 \/><\/span><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  <\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Play Action into the same Run Blitz — the offense wins.<\/strong> You showed run, they bit, and everyone they'd need in coverage is coming downhill instead. <i>Big play. Zone 2 to Zone 4.<\/i><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/extras\/a6d362c119634f44153a3da9cff88e7e.avif?t=1793637442\" width=1000 height=470 \/><\/span><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One card beat that blitz and one card fed it. The ratings barely moved — the difference was the read.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The field is five zones and an end zone, and a series is four plays. Scoring is something you assemble: a touchdown is a run of good calls, and the drive you remember is the one where you won three reads in a row.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/extras\/be5f0d82ab5751999fc76846fecdf7f2.avif?t=1793637442\" width=1000 height=180 \/><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>YOUR PLAYBOOK IS YOUR DECK<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Build your playbook like a coach installs an offense. Earn new plays as your career grows, and rep the ones you trust, plays gain mastery the more you call them, and a play your team has mastered hits harder than one you installed on Tuesday. Scout the opponent's tendencies, check the matchup screen, and bring the right game plan to the right opponent.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every call costs. A per-series token budget means your best looks can't be your every-down looks, the personnel you declare changes what you can afford, and your audibles are a finite resource you can burn early or save for the two-minute drill.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>FOOTBALL, ALL THE WAY DOWN<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Two-point decisions after a late touchdown. Safeties when a stuff goes wrong deep in your own end. Victory formation when you've iced it — or a handshake from a coach who knows you have. If it matters on a real sideline, it matters here.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>If you know football, this game was built for you. <\/strong><\/p>","short_description":"A football strategy card game where you are the coach and the cards are your plays. Level up your coach with perks, use your team's roster to pick the best play possible against your opponent. You manage your team, the recruits, their development from high school to college and the pros.","supported_languages":"English","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/bf87dbd40223c58a6ef3779a1b85ef4288e6f6c0\/header.jpg?t=1793637442","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/cf20b62e32d984db6dd2d09f0cf903f4fd8cc871\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793637442","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5028910\/cf20b62e32d984db6dd2d09f0cf903f4fd8cc871\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793637442","website":"https:\/\/www.cormisys.com\/?utm_source=steam","pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 10 64-bit<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> 64-bit dual-core, 2 GHz<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 4 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Intel UHD 620<br><\/li><li><strong>DirectX:<\/strong> Version 11<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 1 GB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> Minimum 1280×720; 1920×1080 or higher recommended<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<\/li><\/ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Ubuntu 22.04+ \/ SteamOS 3<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> 64-bit dual-core, 2 GHz<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 4 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Vulkan-capable GPU<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 1 GB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> Minimum 1280×720; 1920×1080 or higher recommended<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"developers":["Cormisys"],"publishers":["Cormisys"],"demos":[{"appid":5196430,"description":""}],"price_overview":{"currency":"USD","initial":1999,"final":1799,"discount_percent":10,"initial_formatted":"$19.99","final_formatted":"$17.99"},"packages":[1743886],"package_groups":[{"name":"default","title":"Buy PlayCard Football","description":"","selection_text":"Select a purchase option","save_text":"","display_type":0,"is_recurring_subscription":"false","subs":[{"package